{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650831,"nonce":"iXzkn9bb8sqZOvcm642GtzwDuvw=","title":"Mandible: support multiple agent frameworks (Pi, Claude Code SDK, raw API)","message":"Currently planning Console tab with Claude Code SDK / stream-json integration. We should design the session layer to be framework-agnostic so we can plug in different agent backends.\n\n## Pi framework context\nPi (by Mario Zechner, https://lucumr.pocoo.org/2026/1/31/pi/) is the engine under OpenClaw (217K stars). It is a deliberately minimal coding agent: 4 tools (Read, Write, Edit, Bash), a very short system prompt, an extension system where agents can write and hot-reload their own extensions, and hierarchical session branching. Model-agnostic.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue 0a84807.","files":null}]}